##
   A qualifier on an `impl` block applies to every member.

   `$ impl Counter { ... }` makes the whole block dollar-callable, which is what
   lets its methods run in the VM at all (AGENTS.md 2.10). A member may also
   carry its own qualifier -- `impl Counter { $ func get(...) }` -- when only one
   of them should be, and the two merge rather than clobber, so a member's own
   `$` survives a block that supplies none.

   `extern` works the same way, and shows the extern-C convention marker on the
   emitted function.

   None of this leaves a trace below the frontend. `$ impl Counter { func get }`
   produces MIR and bytecode byte-identical to a hand-written
   `$ func Counter_get(self: Counter)`, and `extern impl` is identical to
   `extern func Counter_get`. `impl_members_accept_qualifiers` and
   `qualified_impl_block_lowers_identically_to_a_hand_written_function` pin both
   halves of that.

   Syntax note: the ABI is a bare identifier or omitted, so it is `extern impl`
   or `extern C impl` -- not `extern "C" impl`, because the ABI token is parsed
   as an identifier, not a string literal.
##
struct Counter { n: i32 }

$ impl Counter {
  func get(self: Counter): i32 { return self.n; }
  func scaled(self: Counter, k: i32): i32 { return self.n * k; }
}

impl Counter {
  $ func doubled(self: Counter): i32 { return self.n * 2i32; }
}

extern impl Counter {
  func cconv(self: Counter): i32 { return self.n; }
}
